GRADING (DFS Rules)
======================================================================

  beta_c(2D) in GZ: YES — physical constant, not derived from GZ.
    Golden Zone range [0.2123, 0.5000] contains the exact Onsager
    solution beta_c = ln(1+sqrt(2))/2 = 0.44069. Both are mathematical
    constants from unrelated derivations. Structural match.
    Fraction of [0,1] covered by GZ = 28.77% -> p(random hit) = 0.2877
    Not a precise equality, therefore: GRADE = 🟧 (weak evidence)

  beta_c(3D) in GZ: YES — MC value 0.22165 barely above lower=0.2123.
    Sits 3.2% up GZ from lower. Very close to boundary.
    p(random hit) = 0.2877 -> no strong evidence alone.
    GRADE = 🟧 (weak evidence, proximity to boundary noted)

  eta(2D) = 1/tau(6): EXACT — no approximation, proven identity.
    eta = 1/4 is proven from Onsager/Yang solution.
    tau(6) = 4 is pure number theory (divisor count).
    GRADE = 🟩 (exact equation, proven)

  delta(2D) = C(6,2): EXACT — 15 = C(6,2), both exact integers.
    delta = 15 proven from scaling law delta = (d+2-eta)/(d-2+eta)
    at d=2, eta=1/4 -> delta = (4-1/4)/(1/4) = (15/4)/(1/4) = 15.
    C(6,2) = 15 is pure combinatorics.
    GRADE = 🟩 (exact equation, both sides independently proven)

  MF beta_c(d=1) = GZ_upper: EXACT — 1/(2*1) = 1/2 = GZ_upper.
    Trivial lattice d=1 mean-field. GZ_upper = 1/2 from Riemann.
    GRADE = 🟩 (exact, but d=1 MF is a degenerate case)

  Summary grades: 🟩 3 exact + 🟧 2 structural (physical constants)
  n=6 arithmetic (tau, C(6,2)) appears in 2D Ising exponents exactly.

